WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.497 --> 00:00:03.503
- [Narrator] In Thailand,

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.861
there are over 40,000 Buddhist temples,

00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:10.861
but there's only one that
looks quite like this.

00:00:12.757 --> 00:00:14.541
Completed in 2004,

00:00:14.541 --> 00:00:18.021
Wat Plai Laem is a collection
of temples and statues

00:00:18.021 --> 00:00:23.017
located on Koh Samui, Thailand's
second largest island.

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:25.493
These are active temples
in a tranquil place

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:27.773
where quiet reflection is encouraged

00:00:27.773 --> 00:00:30.523
and appropriate attire is a must.

00:00:31.478 --> 00:00:33.217
One of the most eye-catching figures

00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:37.027
is the statue of the Buddha,
which is 30 meters high

00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:40.610
and painted in bright
red, white, and gold.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.955
The main statue at Wat Plai Laem

00:00:43.955 --> 00:00:47.874
is the Buddhist goddess of
compassion and mercy, Guan Yin.

00:00:47.874 --> 00:00:50.484
Here, she's represented with 18 arms,

00:00:50.484 --> 00:00:55.269
which shows her ability to help
many people in need at once.

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:58.644
The temple is surrounded by a
lake filled with hungry fish.

00:00:58.644 --> 00:01:00.713
Visitors who make a donation to the temple

00:01:00.713 --> 00:01:02.693
are given a bag of fish food.

00:01:02.693 --> 00:01:05.933
People also buy fish and
turtles at the local food market

00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:08.226
and release them into the lake.

00:01:08.226 --> 00:01:10.853
Buddhists consider it an
act of spiritual merit,

00:01:10.853 --> 00:01:13.603
and the fish and turtles do, too.

